// directory. Byte-range locks already exclude across processes; this map keeps
// two goroutines in this process from racing to create and lock the same
// chain.lock (the loser would, correctly, fail busy — but in-process
// coordination lets a same-process caller queue rather than interleave lock
// metadata writes). Acquisitions still never wait across processes.
